":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":-0.2555384076401006,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.061784474481128594,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":37.3,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.13039911835606163,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.33955983909505494,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.003587239519420782,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":53.6,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.22790479228512855,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.013359999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":8.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc. provides cybersecurity solutions in the United States and internationally. Its unified platform provides cloud-delivered protection of endpoints, cloud workloads, identity, and data through a software as a service (SaaS) subscription-based model. The company offers corporate endpoint and cloud workload security, managed security, security and vulnerability management, IT operations management, identity protection, threat intelligence, data protection, SaaS security posture management, and AI powered workflow automation, and securing generative AI workload services, as well as security orchestration, automation, and response; and security information and event management, and log management services. It primarily sells subscriptions to its Falcon platform and cloud modules. The company has a strategic alliance with Cognizant Technology Solutions Corporation to help enterprises secure artificial intelligence across its lifecycle, from the AI agents and models to the foundational infrastructure that supports the entire AI ecosystem and with Snowflake to bring AI-native security and enterprise data at scale. Additionally, it has a partnership with Fortanix Inc. to combine its Falcon platform with Fortanix Confidential AI to provide an integrated solution for end-to-end AI security. The company was incorporated in 2011 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. George R. Kurtz | Co-Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $5.5M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 11K people. Revenue per employee of $411K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 47%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $112K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $94K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc. is a mega-cap technology business with a $222.1B market cap on $4.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +29% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +4.8pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -14% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 74% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $1.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -16.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -10.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 23% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 1285% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":12.846554149689082},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $65.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Will CRWD's Acquisitions of Fiddler and Dreadnode Boost its AI Growth?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025644/will-crwd-s-acquisitions-of-fiddler-and-dreadnode-boost-its-ai-growth?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cquick_take-3025644","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793975580.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is CrowdStrike Holdings (CRWD) Cheap Following Its AI Kill Switch And Partnership Push?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-crwd/crowdstrike-holdings/news/is-crowdstrike-holdings-crwd-cheap-following-its-ai-kill-swi","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793932604.072,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"CrowdStrike CEO George Kurtz Executes 19,900 Share Sales on Nov. 4-5, 2026 Under 10b5-1 Plan","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/crowdstrike-ceo-george-kurtz-executes-19900-share-sales-on-nov-4-5-2026-under-10b5-1-plan","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793993632.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Deal Dispatch: Salesforce Buys Cresta, CrowdStrike Acquires Two AI Companies, Out West Restaurant Group Bankruptcy","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/m-a/26/11/62998073/deal-dispatch-salesforce-buys-cresta-crowdstrike-acquires-two-ai-companies-out-west-restaurant-group-bankruptcy","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793986619.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Crame